{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\nimport itertools\n\ndef solve():\n    n = int(input().strip())\n    a1, a2, a3 = map(int, input().strip().split())\n    b1, b2, b3 = map(int, input().strip().split())\n    mx = min(a1, b2) + min(a2, b3) + min(a3, b1)\n    temp = 0\n    for per in itertools.permutations([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]):\n        ta1, ta2, ta3 = a1, a2, a3\n        tb1, tb2, tb3 = b1, b2, b3\n        tmx = 0\n        for el in per:\n            if el == 1:\n                t1 = min(ta1, tb1)\n                ta1 -= t1; tb1 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 2:\n                t1 = min(ta1, tb3)\n                ta1 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 3:\n                t1 = min(ta2, tb2)\n                ta2 -= t1; tb2 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 4:\n                t1 = min(ta2, tb1)\n                tb1 -= t1; ta2 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 5:\n                t1 = min(ta3, tb3)\n                ta3 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1\n            elif el == 6:\n                t1 = min(ta3, tb2)\n                tb2 -= t1; ta3 -= t1; tmx += t1\n        temp = max(temp, tmx)\n    print(n - temp, mx)\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    solve()\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 1.0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nvoid solve() {\n    long long n, a1, a2, a3, b1, b2, b3;\n    cin >> n;\n    cin >> a1 >> a2 >> a3;\n    cin >> b1 >> b2 >> b3;\n\n    long long mx = min(a1, b2) + min(a2, b3) + min(a3, b1);\n\n    int perm[6] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6};\n    long long temp = 0;\n    do {\n        long long ta1 = a1, ta2 = a2, ta3 = a3;\n        long long tb1 = b1, tb2 = b2, tb3 = b3;\n        long long tmx = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < 6; ++i) {\n            int el = perm[i];\n            long long t1;\n            if (el == 1) {\n                t1 = min(ta1, tb1);\n                ta1 -= t1; tb1 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n            } else if (el == 2) {\n                t1 = min(ta1, tb3);\n                ta1 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n            } else if (el == 3) {\n                t1 = min(ta2, tb2);\n                ta2 -= t1; tb2 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n            } else if (el == 4) {\n                t1 = min(ta2, tb1);\n                tb1 -= t1; ta2 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n            } else if (el == 5) {\n                t1 = min(ta3, tb3);\n                ta3 -= t1; tb3 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n            } else if (el == 6) {\n                t1 = min(ta3, tb2);\n                tb2 -= t1; ta3 -= t1; tmx += t1;\n            }\n        }\n        temp = max(temp, tmx);\n    } while (next_permutation(perm, perm + 6));\n\n    cout << n - temp << \" \" << mx << endl;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    solve();\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-7.033323527139146e-06, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0003599472693167627, -0.00014423283573705703, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -5.149708886165172e-05, 0.0, 0.